A||N||5||kornholio||floor lights stay on with a buzzing sound||||8||
Z||000000||kornholio||08-14-2000||06:10 AM||||Here's my problem:<BR>I'm driving and my floor lights come on dimly with a buzzing sound coming from the passenger footwell.  The buzzing goes away if I flip the dimmer switch all the way up to turn on the map lights.  There is no light at all coming from the map lights.  If I flip the dimmer back to normal position, the buzzing starts again.  With the dimmer in the normal driving position, the buzzing will go away if I open the door.  If I push the door pin the buzzing starts again.  Any ideas?<BR>Thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||kornholio||08-14-2000||06:30 AM||||nevermind, found the problem||||reg||14
Z||000002||Carrolles||08-14-2000||08:19 AM||||I'm having a similar problem on the 85GT I just bought.  The map lights won't come on but each of the three map light switchs will turn on the footwell lights.  The map light bulbs are good because I removed the fixture and powered it up on the work bench.  I suspect I have a faulty ground somewhere.<P>What did you find to be the problem?<P>TIA,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-14-2000||12:55 PM||||I have one of the 3 switch light consoles.  Since one of the fixtures for the center light is broken, I removed the bulbs from the center lights.  I installed blue (couldn't find purple) lights in my footwells (stock locations).  Now, when I push the button for the center lights, all that comes on are the blue footwell lights.  Cool blue glow without the expense (and wiring hassles) of neon.  The map lights still work individually.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||08-14-2000||02:11 PM||||check your BATT fuse.  I had a similar issue last week.  The footwell lights would only come on with a buzzing sound when the horn was pressed.||||reg||1
Z||000005||kornholio||08-14-2000||06:54 PM||||It turns out that it was my power door lock kit that I installed.  The relay for it was faulty, that's what was causing the buzzing. And for the map lights not working, it was a blown fuse.||||reg||1
